        <mxCell id="0fp3uru1z_SA0XE15nQW-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Typically, the higher layer commands the lower layer. For example, the Grid planning gives a grid path that the motion planning tree can grow along.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;However, the Action planning layer can also speak directly to the Motion planning layer, and skip the Grid planning layer. For example, when in combat, the Action given from the Action layer directly controls the Motion planning layer. The player moves more precisely in a small space as a result.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
